**IRWB-020-K stage 1 is complete.** [Ticket](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-020-K--tix-language-tensor-ir-evaluators-meaning-contract-and-passes/index.md) · [Revised design](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-020-K--tix-language-tensor-ir-evaluators-meaning-contract-and-passes/design-doc/01-tix-stage-1-design.md) · [Diary](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-020-K--tix-language-tensor-ir-evaluators-meaning-contract-and-passes/reference/01-diary.md)

- `src/tensor/` implements Tix parsing and checking, the v6 tensor IR, f32 and f64 evaluation, and the checked `inline` and `split-sum` passes. The build exports exactly `compileTix`, `runTix`, and `optimizeTix`.
- `corpus/tensor/` contains matmul, max-shifted softmax, layernorm, single-head attention, tanh-GELU MLP, and NCHW conv2d. `tests/tensor/` checks all six against independent formulas.
- The nine-element witness produced `0x3f900000` before `split-sum` and `0x3f900002` after it. Exact rejected the candidate; tolerance accepted it. Both deliberately wrong rewrites reached the real gate and were rejected.

**Framework change:** `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts` adds a native-only mode so read-only adapters need no edit draft, and `applyNativePassSync` so `optimizeTix` can check candidates synchronously. Both paths share candidate validation, diffing, correspondence, and write checks. No contract-layer changes were needed.

**Refinement to the revised design:** `inline` skips substitutions whose composed affine access cannot be represented or proven in bounds. The attention corpus uses `sqrt(max(D,1))` to keep zero-width heads finite.

